       indicate the error.

       If  _m_o_d_e is LLIIOO__WWAAIITT, lliioo__lliissttiioo() returns 0 when all of the I/O opera‐
       tions have completed successfully.  Otherwise, -1 is returned, and  _e_r_‐
       _r_n_o is set to indicate the error.

       The return status from lliioo__lliissttiioo() provides information only about the
       call  itself,  not about the individual I/O operations.  One or more of
       the I/O operations may fail, but this does not prevent other operations
